payload.summary:
As of 14 May 2024, Qorvo v. Akoustis (D. Del. 1:21-cv-01417) is in jury trial (Day 1 on 6 May, Day 7 on 14 May). Akoustis says a verdict is expected within days. No verdict or judgment has been entered.

Claims before the jury:
- trade secrets, civil conspiracy, Lanham Act false advertising, NC UDTPA and infringement of the '018/'755 patents;
- patent validity was settled for Qorvo on summary judgment (D.I. 557);
- the RICO and false-marking counts were disposed of (D.I. 545).

Qorvo's statement of intended proof seeks:
- $66.1M head-start unjust enrichment, asserted identically under trade secret, UDTPA and conspiracy;
- $809,772 recruiting costs, $1,146,604 corrective advertising and $279,808 patent royalty;
- exemplary/treble/punitive damages, fees, interest and an injunction.

Akoustis's position:
- it contests all liability and damages;
- its damages expert (Irwin) uses avoided costs (figure redacted);
- it argues the conspiracy remedy duplicates trade-secret damages.

Court rulings on damages evidence:
- the Daubert challenges to both damages experts were denied (D.I. 553), and whether all historical revenue belongs in the base was left to the jury;
- on 14 May (D.I. 590) the court granted Akoustis's Rule 50(a) motion in part: no compensable UDTPA damages, though injury may be found.

Akoustis's General Counsel said an eight-figure verdict is possible.

10-Q disclosures:
- $15.2M cash at 31 March 2024;
- substantial going-concern doubt; an adverse judgment could force curtailment or a voluntary bankruptcy petition;
- no litigation accrual;
- $48.0M of ATM capacity and no other funding commitments.

Other capital-markets facts:
- The January 2024 offering sold 23M shares at $0.50 (Roth) for $10.4M net.
- Nasdaq bid-price compliance is due by 21 October 2024; the stock closed at $0.44 on 14 May.
- The $44.0M 6.0% notes default on unpaid, unstayed final judgments above $10.0M after 60 days and notice. They also default on delisting, which is a fundamental change giving holders a cash repurchase right. Holders of 25% may accelerate.
